            <ArticleTitle>Strategies to reduce children's perception of pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>34-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain is one of the most complex of all human stressors. This paper reviews the literature specific to children's pain and outlines the factors that influence how they perceive pain. The author also describes how children's pain is observed and how their needs are met in his own unit, and the importance of involving children in the management of their pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
